@startuml
left to right direction

"Application Publisher/\nLibrary Developer/\nCorDapp publisher" as APP_PUB #LightGreen 
"System/Infra\n Operator" as INFRA_OP #LightGreen 
"Network\n Operator" as NET_OP #LightGreen 
"CorDapp\n User" as CORDAPP_USER #LightPink
"VNode\n Operator/\nGroup member/\nPeer member/\nCounterparty " as VNODE_OP #LightPink 
"Cluster\n Operator" as CLUSTER_OP #Yellow 
"Notary Operator" as NOT_OP #LightGreen
"Anonymous" as ANON  #red
'participant "\nMGM\n Cluster\n" as MGM order 70 #LightGreen 
'participant "\nMember\n Cluster\n" as MEMBER order 2 #LightCoral 
'participant "\nNotary\n Cluster\n" as NOTARY order 80 #LightGreen
'participant "\nPeer\n Cluster\n" as PEER order 90 #red
'participant "Certificate Authority \n +OSCP" as CA order 100
'skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center


'hide footbo

'skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
'hide unlinked
NET_OP --> (Manages MGM)
(Manages MGM) -->( Initialize and maintain a Application Network:\n signs CPIs, accepts member requests, etc)
(Manages MGM) --> (Uploads its own Session/Identity certificate for P2P communications)
(Manages MGM) --> (request the CSR -certificate signing request- for its own identity) 
(Manages MGM) --> (generate a CSR for a tenant)


INFRA_OP --> (Install...\ncluster, Kafka, VNode DB, cluster DB, K8s workers,\n load balancers, Proxies,\n Access K8 APIs, DBs networks, hardware...)

APP_PUB --> (Distribute his public key/sign certificate)
APP_PUB --> (Create, sign and publish CPKs and CPBs)

VNODE_OP --> (Joins an Application Network)

(Joins an Application Network) --> (Retrieves the group policy from the MGM)
'(Joins an Application Network) --> (checks the statuses of all registration requests for a specified holding identity)
(Joins an Application Network) --> (checks the status of the specified\n registration request for a holding identity)
(Joins an Application Network) --> (configures a holding identity as a network participant\n by setting properties required for P2P messaging)
VNODE_OP --> (Discovers Application Network members)
(Discovers Application Network members) --> (Retrieves a list of all active and \npending members in the membership group)
NOT_OP --> (Manages notary service)
CORDAPP_USER --> (Call the Flow REST API on a specific VNode)
CORDAPP_USER --> (Call and retrieve CordApp Flows)
(Call and retrieve CordApp Flows) --> (Get all flows that can be used by the specified holding identity)
(Call and retrieve CordApp Flows) --> (Start a new instance for the specified flow for the specified holding identity)
(Call and retrieve CordApp Flows) --> (Get the current status of the specified flow instance)
CLUSTER_OP --> (Register a VNode\nstarts the registration process for a holding identity)

CLUSTER_OP --> (Upload and manages CPI)
(Upload and manages CPI) --> (upload a CPI file to the Corda cluster) 
(Upload and manages CPI) --> (list of all CPIs uploaded to the cluster)
(Upload and manages CPI) --> (Get the status information for the CPI upload with the given request ID)
(Upload and manages CPI) --> (overwrite the previously stored CPI record. \nThis operation also purges any sandboxes running)
CLUSTER_OP --> (Configure Cluster certificates \nP2P, RPC API, CPI code signing checks)
'imports a certificate chain for a cluster. TODO: fix API DOC API DOC
'gets the certificate chain aliases for a cluster. API doc and other get APIs methods
CLUSTER_OP --> (request the CSR for its own identity)
CLUSTER_OP --> (enables to generate a CSR for a tenant \n (cluster tenant TLS: rpc-api or P2P)
CLUSTER_OP --> (apply and read Cluster level configurations)
(apply and read Cluster level configurations) --> (updates a section of the cluster configuration)
(apply and read Cluster level configurations) --> (returns the 'active' configuration for the given section,\n in both the 'raw' format and with defaults applied)
CLUSTER_OP --> (Manages HSMs :'ACCOUNTS', 'CI', \n'LEDGER', 'NOTARY', 'SESSION_INIT',\n 'TLS', or 'JWT_KEY')
(Manages HSMs :'ACCOUNTS', 'CI', \n'LEDGER', 'NOTARY', 'SESSION_INIT',\n 'TLS', or 'JWT_KEY') --> (assign a soft HSM to the tenant for the specified category)
(Manages HSMs :'ACCOUNTS', 'CI', \n'LEDGER', 'NOTARY', 'SESSION_INIT',\n 'TLS', or 'JWT_KEY') --> (retrieves information on the HSM of the specified category assigned to the tenant)
(Manages HSMs :'ACCOUNTS', 'CI', \n'LEDGER', 'NOTARY', 'SESSION_INIT',\n 'TLS', or 'JWT_KEY') --> (enables to assign a hardware-backed HSM to the tenant for the specified category)
CLUSTER_OP --> (Create Cluster level Key Pairs)
(Create Cluster level Key Pairs) --> (generates a new key pair for a tenant -cluster tenant being rpc-api or p2p)
(Create Cluster level Key Pairs) --> (Setup permissions and RBAC)
(Setup permissions and RBAC) --> (creates a new permission. https://CLUSTER/api/v1/permission)
(Setup permissions and RBAC) --> (creates a set of permissions bulk \nand optionally assigns them to the existing roles/n https://CLUSTER/api/v1/permission/bulk)
(Setup permissions and RBAC) --> (creates a new role in the RBAC permission system\n https://CLUSTER/api/v1/role)
(Setup permissions and RBAC) --> (adds the specified permission to the specified role \n https://CLUSTER/api/v1/role/{roleid}/permission/{permissionid})
(Setup permissions and RBAC) --> (removes the specified permission from the specified role.)
(Setup permissions and RBAC) --> (creates a new user with initialPassword, roles, optional SSO ...)
(Setup permissions and RBAC) --> (assigns a specified role to a specified user)
(Setup permissions and RBAC) --> (removes the specified role from the specified user)
CLUSTER_OP --> (Creates and list VNodes)
(Creates and list VNodes) --> (creates a new virtual node)
(Creates and list VNodes) --> (lists all virtual nodes in the cluster)
(Creates and list VNodes) --> (updates the state of a new virtual node to one of the pre-defined values)
@enduml